nit RAM ceiling: verify 64GB is actually reachable

cld-strand-astro-serving.md (Drive, 2026-08-15) assumes nit "eventually wants
64GB" for the processing role. nit is deliberately AM4/DDR4 (32G DDR4 beat 16G
DDR5 in the price crisis). Before that ceiling is treated as a plan, check the
board's DIMM count, how many slots are populated now, and the max supported
capacity per slot — 64GB on 2 populated slots means replacing DIMMs, not adding
them. Also re-check B550 M.2/SATA lane sharing while the spec is open.
